Bioqore lab tools: media make-up (idea credit)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Sources (ideas only):
  - github.com/Bioqore/lab_tools (commit 0151377), media_calculator.py:
    stock volumes from C1*V1 = C2*V2 for a recipe at a fixed final volume.
  - github.com/Bioqore/d2_diagrams (commit b77d15b), Lab/lab_tools.d2:
    the "media calculator" step in the lab workflow.
  - github.com/Bioqore/ad_hoc_data_analyses (commit 82e6ae0), the "Stock
    Solutions" sheet of a batch ticket: that stocks are declared per component
    with a unit (sheet name and unit only; no values were read or copied).

What was adapted: idea credit; re-implemented, no code copied. Kalos's
kalos/analysis/makeup.py computes the same quantity with exact decimal
arithmetic, unit conversion (mass, % w/v, and molar with a declared molecular
weight) and refusals (negative water, stock too dilute, unit mismatch without a
molecular weight, missing or duplicated stocks) where the source script skipped
or zero-filled those cases.
